  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>40</x>
      <y>1159</y>
      <w>780</w>
      <h>164</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Persistence design decisions
* Repository pattern: one repository per aggregate/table, sharing generic CRUD in BaseJdbcRepository.
* Single-table inheritance: User, Customer, InteriorDesigner and Admin all persist to 'users';
  discriminator column = role (CUSTOMER / ID / ADMIN).
* BaseEntity is a mapped superclass: created_at / updated_at are copied into each child table.
* companies.owner_user_id is UNIQUE, which enforces the 1:1 InteriorDesigner-Company rule.
* favourites has UNIQUE(user_id, project_id) so a project is favourited once per customer.
* project_views.user_id is nullable: anonymous views are tracked via session_id.
* Project -&gt; ProjectImage is a composition: images are removed together with their project.
* All DB access goes through ConnectionManager (pooled connections, explicit transactions).
bg=#fff2cc
fontsize=10</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
